# Cosign Public Key for URLCleanseBot

## Keyless Signing (OIDC) - Recommended Verification

URLCleanseBot uses **keyless signing** with GitHub Actions OIDC tokens. There is no static public key file. Instead, verification is done using the certificate's identity and OIDC issuer.

### Verify Container Image Signature

```bash
# Verify the container image signature
cosign verify \
  --certificate-identity-regexp "https://github.com/good-wine/urlcleansebot/.github/workflows/.*" \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer "https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com" \
  ghcr.io/good-wine/urlcleansebot@v0.2.0
```

### Verify Container Image SBOM Attestation

```bash
# Verify SPDX SBOM attestation
cosign verify-attestation \
  --type spdxjson \
  --certificate-identity-regexp "https://github.com/good-wine/urlcleansebot/.github/workflows/.*" \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer "https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com" \
  ghcr.io/good-wine/urlcleansebot@v0.2.0

# Verify CycloneDX SBOM attestation
cosign verify-attestation \
  --type cyclonedxjson \
  --certificate-identity-regexp "https://github.com/good-wine/urlcleansebot/.github/workflows/.*" \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer "https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com" \
  ghcr.io/good-wine/urlcleansebot@v0.2.0
```

### Verify SLSA Provenance

```bash
cosign verify-attestation \
  --type slsaprovenance \
  --certificate-identity-regexp "https://github.com/good-wine/urlcleansebot/.github/workflows/.*" \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer "https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com" \
  ghcr.io/good-wine/urlcleansebot@v0.2.0
```

### Verify Release Binary (from GitHub Releases)

```bash
# Download the binary and signature files from the release
gh release download v0.2.0 --repo good-wine/urlcleansebot \
  -p "url_cleanse_bot" -p "url_cleanse_bot.sig" -p "url_cleanse_bot.pem"

# Verify the binary
cosign verify-blob \
  --certificate url_cleanse_bot.pem \
  --signature url_cleanse_bot.sig \
  --certificate-identity-regexp "https://github.com/good-wine/urlcleansebot/.github/workflows/.*" \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer "https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com" \
  url_cleanse_bot
```

### Verify SBOM Files (from GitHub Releases)

```bash
# Download SBOM and signatures
gh release download v0.2.0 --repo good-wine/urlcleansebot \
  -p "sbom.spdx.json" -p "sbom.spdx.json.sig" -p "sbom.spdx.json.pem" \
  -p "sbom.cyclonedx.json" -p "sbom.cyclonedx.json.sig" -p "sbom.cyclonedx.json.pem"

# Verify SPDX SBOM
cosign verify-blob \
  --certificate sbom.spdx.json.pem \
  --signature sbom.spdx.json.sig \
  --certificate-identity-regexp "https://github.com/good-wine/urlcleansebot/.github/workflows/.*" \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer "https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com" \
  sbom.spdx.json

# Verify CycloneDX SBOM
cosign verify-blob \
  --certificate sbom.cyclonedx.json.pem \
  --signature sbom.cyclonedx.json.sig \
  --certificate-identity-regexp "https://github.com/good-wine/urlcleansebot/.github/workflows/.*" \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer "https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com" \
  sbom.cyclonedx.json
```

### Verify Provenance (from GitHub Releases)

```bash
gh release download v0.2.0 --repo good-wine/urlcleansebot \
  -p "provenance.intoto.jsonl" -p "provenance.intoto.jsonl.sig" -p "provenance.intoto.jsonl.pem"

cosign verify-blob \
  --certificate provenance.intoto.jsonl.pem \
  --signature provenance.intoto.jsonl.sig \
  --certificate-identity-regexp "https://github.com/good-wine/urlcleansebot/.github/workflows/.*" \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer "https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com" \
  provenance.intoto.jsonl
```

### Verify Checksums (from GitHub Releases)

```bash
gh release download v0.2.0 --repo good-wine/urlcleansebot \
  -p "checksums.txt" -p "checksums.txt.sig" -p "checksums.txt.pem"

cosign verify-blob \
  --certificate checksums.txt.pem \
  --signature checksums.txt.sig \
  --certificate-identity-regexp "https://github.com/good-wine/urlcleansebot/.github/workflows/.*" \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer "https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com" \
  checksums.txt

# Then verify the checksums match
sha256sum -c checksums.txt
```

## Key Information

- **Certificate Identity Pattern**: `https://github.com/good-wine/urlcleansebot/.github/workflows/*`
- **OIDC Issuer**: `https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com`
- **Registry**: `ghcr.io/good-wine/urlcleansebot`
- **Signing Method**: Keyless (GitHub Actions OIDC)

## Why Keyless?

Keyless signing eliminates private key management:
- No long-lived private keys to rotate or compromise
- Each signature is bound to a specific workflow run
- Full audit trail via GitHub Actions logs
- Short-lived certificates (valid ~10 minutes)
- Transparency log (Rekor) entry for each signature

## If You Need a Static Public Key

For environments that require a static public key, you can extract it from a certificate:

```bash
# Extract public key from a certificate
openssl x509 -in url_cleanse_bot.pem -pubkey -noout > cosign.pub
```

However, **keyless verification with certificate identity is strongly preferred** as it provides stronger supply chain guarantees.